===Climate===
[[File:Shiogami Yuzu Grove.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Yuzu groves on the slopes of Mount Shiogami, benefiting from the prefecture's subtropical climate.]]

Shiogami Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification ''Cfa''), with warm, wet summers and mild, relatively dry winters. The island chain's position in the southern Shendan Ocean means it receives abundant sunshine year-round, a critical factor in both its salt production heritage and its citrus cultivation. Summer temperatures regularly exceed 30 °C (86 °F), while winter temperatures rarely fall below 8 °C (46 °F) at sea level.

The prefecture is within the typhoon belt, and severe tropical storms frequently strike between November and April. The mountainous interior of the main island provides some shelter to the leeward coastal communities, but the smaller outer islands are fully exposed. Annual precipitation ranges from approximately 1,800 mm on the main island to over 2,200 mm on the windward southern islands.

